WEBVTT

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.530
<b>Haneda International Airport</b>

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.450
<b>Heisei 2</b>

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.750
<b>7/25/2017</b>

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.560
I can't wait, can you, Shindo-san?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.810
Why, Hanamori?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.770
It's been forever since we got to leave the country!

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.600
<b>Hanamori Shun</b>

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.600
Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Policy Bureau
 United Nations Policy Division Officer

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.100
It's an international conference!

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.060
Hey!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:48.940
Sir!

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.860
Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Policy Bureau 
United Nations Policy Division Officer

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.860
<b>Shindo Kojiro</b>

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.200
Aw, jeez... wait, Shindo-san!

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.130
What is this?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.300
Oh, this is from that thing...

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.600
Osakabe Plating

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.720
But that's Shindo-san for you, isn't it?

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.100
I never thought a land-buying 
job would end up like that.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.190
Don't get the wrong idea,

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.650
I wasn't asked to buy anything.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.110
What was it, then?

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.400
A negotiation.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.490
Negotiation?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.910
Getting what's in your interest 
is the goal of negotiations.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.460
But defeating your opponent and 
temporarily gaining what you want

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.130
will always come back to 
bite you in the long term.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.170
What's best for you is giving both 
parties something in their interest.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.720
It's easy to say,

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.850
but it's really hard to do, isn't it?

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.470
There isn't just one answer, for one thing.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.560
We aren't God.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:16.070
We'll never know what was right—and what 
was the right answer—for our whole lives.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:20.280
But, even if we don't know, 
we just have to keep looking.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.160
Shindo-san?

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.120
What is that?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.300
Sir, please remain in your seat.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.640
Sir!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.010
What is that?

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.220
It's getting bigger!

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.310
Captain, the passengers 
are starting to panic.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.230
Isn't it dangerous to take off?

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.360
Cancel the takeoff.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.160
We're going to temporarily move to runway A.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.110
Control,

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.410
<i>this is flight 256.</i>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.080
<i>Repeat.</i>

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.160
<i>Cancel the takeoff.</i>

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.580
<i>Cancel the takeoff.</i>

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.250
<i>We're temporarily moving to runway A.</i>

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.070
Sir, please get back to your seat!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.470
What is this, Shindo-san?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.800
Get back, Hanamori!

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.430
What? What?

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.680
Shindo-san!

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.560
I can't get it off! I can't get it off!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.890
Calm down, Hanamori!

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:15.900
Captain!

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:27.620
Help me! Help me, Shindo-san!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.120
Hanamori!

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.590
Flight 256, this is control.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.300
Can you hear me? Come in!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.680
Flight 256, this is control.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.850
Can you hear me? Come in!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:49.970
Come in!

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:14.100
<b>Kasumigaseki</b>

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.550
<b>Cabinet Secretariat National Security Agency</b>

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.200
A cube?

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.780
Cabinet Secretariat 
National Security Agency 
Information Team  <b>Natsume Ritsu</b>

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.290
Supposedly, but it's hard to say for sure.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.790
Any images of it?

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.180
There's several of them going around online.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.390
<b>Haneda Cube</b>

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.830
It's a cube, yeah.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.380
An incredibly big one.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.800
Haneda's going to be out 
of commission for a while.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.840
If we're too slow in dealing 
with this, it'll be the end of us.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.380
I'll gather information.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:50.140
Councilor, one of the planes on
 the runway has gone missing.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.980
Missing?

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:52.890
Yes.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.900
It's believed to be where
 the huge object appeared.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.570
So both it and the passengers were crushed?

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:02.650
I'll draw up a passenger list for now.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.650
I'll help.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.400
Thanks.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.700
I'll send you the files.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.720
<b>You have mail.</b>

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.730
Kikuchi Daiki 
Kojiro Shindo 
Shun Hanamori

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.170
Shindo-kun?

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:21.690
The first news broadcasts are starting!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.150
<i>Breaking news.</i>

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.890
<i>Around 10:00 AM this morning,</i>

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:32.870
<b><i>Breaking News:</i></b>

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:32.870
<b>Huge Building Appears At Haneda International</b>

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.850
<i>something that appears to be a huge building</i>

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:32.890
<i>appeared on the runways of Haneda Airport.</i>

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:36.850
Gonno-san?

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.190
What is that?

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.110
We're going to film it and find out.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.900
Is it dangerous?

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.280
We're going to find that out, too!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:49.720
NNK Broadcasting Director  <b>Gonno Takumi</b>

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.450
We'll have to do this before they censor it.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.720
Gonno-san.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.800
Hey, we're too close!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.080
It's just that big.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.450
We're still a distance away.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.000
What next?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.790
Go up. Get us higher.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.380
First I want a shot of the whole thing.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.340
Up, huh?

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.760
Read out our height in meters.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.680
Is the camera ready?

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:09.550
Yup.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.680
Okay, patch us in.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.850
We're above the scene.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.140
We are presently

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:20.520
flying alongside the mysterious, massive 
object that appeared out of nowhere.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.020
What's our present altitude?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.400
1700 meters.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.090
1700 meters!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.900
It's huge!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.550
But we still can't see the top.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.010
1800 meters.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.290
What a strange wall.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:37.640
It's not clear if it's artificial or natural.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.100
1900 meters.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.640
The helicopter keeps going up.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:45.050
The mysterious wall just keeps going.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:46.650
2000 meters!

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:54.390
We've come out on top of the wall.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:55.770
It's a perfect square...

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.740
A cube!

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:03.150
It's a massive cube, two kilometers per side!

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.460
<b>Nagata-cho, Prime Minister's Residence</b>

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:17.750
I'd like to begin our conference on how to

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:20.290
Chief Cabinet Secretary  <b>Ubuka Kiyotaka</b>

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:22.350
deal with the mysterious, large object 
that has appeared at Haneda Airport.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.750
First, let's have a report on the 
present situation from all ministries.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.550
Transportation has been affected,

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.150
but the people of the city 
are remaining calm.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:35.510
We aren't planning on any 
censorship at the present stage.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:38.480
We'll tell them to avoid 
panicking the citizens,

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.440
but we're leaving the media to 
report the facts as they are,

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.110
and sharing information 
with them as necessary.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.570
At the present, we have
 very little information.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:52.510
What we need first is accurate 
information gathering.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:55.080
I'll go over what we know now.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:01.370
First, the object is a perfect cube, 
approximately two kilometers a side.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.040
Appeared at 10:05 
2 Km per side

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:06.630
In addition, at the Haneda Terminal 
Building approximately 500 meters away,

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:09.360
no radiation, nor anything 
similar, has been detected.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.970
So, we can get closer?

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:14.300
It's dangerous to act without all the facts.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.260
First, we should have the police and 
fire department confirm its safety—

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.140
Have there been any causalities so far?

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:23.940
We haven't seen any major 
damage near the object.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.690
However, we have information 
that one passenger plane

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.940
was crushed by the object when it appeared.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:34.950
How many people were aboard?

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.930
252 people.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.270
We still don't know.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.890
Play this.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:01.930
Here, let me.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.890
Who are you?

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.400
Sorry, Ubuka-san.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.580
My assistant is...

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.190
Mifune-sensei.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:11.690
Professor of Physics  <b>Mifune Tetsuto</b>

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.110
I was here for a conference,

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:14.570
but I was asked for my opinion on that.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.590
It makes contact with the plane here.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.790
But, the plane doesn't seem to feel any impact

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.040
and doesn't slow down.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.410
It doesn't seem to cling to it, really.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:28.020
It's like water, but even if it were gelatinous, 
there would be more resistance.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.090
We still don't know, so we 
can come back to that later.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.550
But basically, it's not that hard.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:36.260
Anyway, at this point,
 the whole thing is absorbed.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.260
At this time, the plane's going 
about 22 meters per second,

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.060
and there's about 800 meters 
to go until this edge.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.940
If nothing happened, it should
 have popped out really quick.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:45.770
But, it doesn't.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.270
Something happened.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.020
What's going on inside?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:52.110
Well, we can investigate that later.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:56.280
Anyway, what's important here is that 
this plane might not be that damaged.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.300
So they...

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.470
Theoretical Physicist   <b>Shinawa Kanata</b>

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.470
might still be alive.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.330
What?

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.000
Prime Minister.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:13.630
Prime Minister   <b>Inuzuka Kozo</b>

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.500
Our primary objective is 
rescuing the passengers.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:53.060
National Police Agency Commissioner's Secretariat
National Public Safety Commission
 Assistant Executive Aide

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:53.060
<b>Asano Shuhei</b>

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.170
What's the situation?

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:53.080
The airport's been successfully sealed off.

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:56.630
It's an emergency situation, so we 
were able to get enough people.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.570
The problem is...

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:03.280
Whether or not the police and fire departments
 can actually do anything about that.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.140
A response HQ will be 
established here by nightfall.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.430
The JSDF's Intelligence and Security divisions

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.870
have been sent messages,

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.100
but no official order has been given to them.

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:15.040
If we waste too much time, the passengers...

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:16.860
I'm aware.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:22.450
Shindo...

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.250
Let's go!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.210
Dr. Shinawa!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.190
Dr. Shinawa!

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:44.180
What?

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.760
Send drones first, please.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.310
Oh, right.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:04.610
No EM radiation. No particle radiation.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:05.530
What about Doppler?

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.370
Not coming back.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.700
Thermal?

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.500
I don't know.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.500
What is this?

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.390
Is it cold?

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.540
Is it absolute zero?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.340
I don't think that's right, but...

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.170
It's giving off no infrared radiation at all?

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.260
That's amazing on its own.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.140
So, what are we looking at?

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.260
Is it really visible light?

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.370
If it wasn't, we couldn't see it.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.080
It's important to confirm the obvious, right?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:40.110
It's getting close, but 
nothing's happening, huh?

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.610
I could go right until I hit it...

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.630
Okay, do it!

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.990
I'm sorry. It's expensive.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.620
Can we make contact with this?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.250
I can destroy this one, right?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:59.310
No, this one isn't cheap, either...

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:11.600
Can we get closer?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:12.450
Yes.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.910
Is it like a ferrofluid?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:19.610
Is it applying some force to 
a liquid to make it transform?

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:23.110
Also the boundaries are oddly clear.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.630
Is there some kind of membrane over it?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.620
Should I take a sample?

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:29.760
Yeah.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.330
This is...

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.550
"Fregonics."

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.680
This is the name we came up with for now!

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.580
What is that?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.450
Incredible isolation!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:20.830
We tried a lot of things, 
but nothing goes through.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:20.830
Construction Vehicle

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.000
First Contact

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.090
Disaster Monitoring Robot

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.090
Perfect isolation and separation.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.500
Heat From Lighting Truck

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.000
It's awful!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.930
Water

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.380
We still don't know what principle 
the isolation is using,

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.260
Bucket Shovel

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:31.300
Circular Saw

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.820
so we need to keep investigating.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.510
Dry Ice

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.450
It may have entirely different 
physical properties.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:33.450
Construction Vehicle

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.810
In other words, breaking 
that wall is impossible?

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.480
I wouldn't go that far.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.040
We might be able to do it if we try harder.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.730
But, I can tell you that at this point, 
everything we've tried has failed.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:48.570
Seems like overtechnology, huh?

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:52.570
Well, we don't know if 
it's even technology at all.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:56.740
If we can't break that wall,

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.370
what happens to the passengers?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.630
If we assume they're all alive,

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:09.010
the passenger plane contains two days 
worth of food and 1200 liters of water.

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:12.590
If they all share it,

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.310
they might not last two weeks.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:22.900
Some of the passengers are children. 
They may not last as long...

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.940
Excuse me.

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:24.770
Message from the response HQ.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:26.150
Send it through.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:30.740
Hello? This is the risk management center.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.780
This is the local response...

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.620
Give us your orders!

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:37.370
Dr. Shinawa!

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.620
We'll work even harder!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:50.470
<b>Japan Ground Self-Defense Force   Camp Asaka</b>

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:09.130
I never thought we'd ever
 use our guns in Tokyo.

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:09.130
JGSDF Sergeant   <b>Agata Atsuhiko</b>

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:20.660
For now, we're going to try using as 
much kinetic energy as we possibly can.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:26.330
And so, I'd like to try 
using the... AP rounds?

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:29.250
Which have the most penetrating 
power of all tank rounds.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:34.880
At a distance of two kilometers, they can 
penetrate 600 millimeters of metal armor.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.490
We're going to assume this squishy 
stuff is more powerful than metal armor

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:41.200
Repair Factory Station

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:41.200
Domestic Terminal 1

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.200
and get close...

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.620
We don't know whether it's 
 solid or empty inside,

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.610
but either way, we're going 
to aim at the thinnest point,

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:48.860
the corner.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:51.570
If the tank shell works in the slightest,

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.840
it'll give us a hint as to how 
to save the people inside,

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.240
and if we can chip off a bit of the surface,

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.280
we'll be able to analyze it.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.990
Plus, it's an experiment we can do quick

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.870
as long as we've got a tank, 
a shell, and permission!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:05.540
It's a win-win-win of a 
wonderful operation, right?

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:10.800
However, if even this amount of 
kinetic energy fails to do anything...

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:11.960
If it does?

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:16.820
It may be impossible for 
humanity for a while.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.390
Shindo-kun...

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:43.240
The shell weighs 7800 grams,

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.330
and leaves the barrel at 
6000 kilometers an hour,

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.640
so the energy amount is over 1000 megajoules.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:52.130
If it survives this unharmed 
it's really gotta be a god! A god!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.470
Preparations are complete.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.310
Go ahead and fire.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:05.120
Target, cube to the front!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.810
Type: AP shell!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.080
Fire!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.290
What was the result?

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.710
Hit...

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.670
It's a god!

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.530
No...

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.470
What's that?

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.120
What?

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:48.700
What is it?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.630
What is this?

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.670
Shindo-kun!

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:40.450
That asshole.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.290
Is that...

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.240
Fregonics...

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.380
Mankind...

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:38.380
I am Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:05.130
Yaha-kui zaShunina

00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:39.580
<i>We'll appoint a government delegation 
and select a negotiator.</i>

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:41.480
<i>What am I looking at?</i>

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:43.270
<i>Something supernatural?</i>

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:46.040
<i>Shindo-san!</i>

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:51.000
Novo
